{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, upon machalat</b> — Some say: machalat is from the root חל\"ל (profane), like במכסת (in the numbering). This is not correct, for במכסת is in construct state. The correct interpretation is [that it refers to] the piyyut beginning מחלת משכיל, [by] No'am, which I have already explained. Rabbi Moses says: \"The villain says in his heart\" — because his way has corrupted him. The correct interpretation in my eyes: the matter is reversed, and first he speaks in singular, then in plural — he sins and causes others to sin."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:43.822442134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}